WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.709
This is Coding Exercise 1 You need one row
containing three different

00:00:05.735 --> 00:00:12.256
counts from admissions all admissions completed
admissions and unique patients Think

00:00:12.282 --> 00:00:17.417
carefully about which COUNT expression answers each
question One measure should count

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:22.956
every row One should count only known discharge
times One should

00:00:22.982 --> 00:00:28.576
count distinct patient identifiers Complete the SQL
directly in

00:00:28.589 --> 00:00:33.988
the browser and select Run and Check Before you run
it predict

00:00:34.014 --> 00:00:36.659
which of the three numbers should be largest and
which should be

00:00:36.672 --> 00:00:42.248
smallest If the SQL runs but does not pass inspect
the column

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:46.514
aliases and the meaning of each count Do not replace
the query

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.198
with a memorized answer Use the definitions from the
COUNT section to

00:00:51.224 --> 00:00:52.198
correct your work
